<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.IO</RootNamespace>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.BinaryData</AssemblyName>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU;x64</Platforms>
    <Configurations>Debug;Release;LipidSearch;Rsharp_app_release;PlantMAT;mzkit;NPSearch;mzkit_win32;gcmodeller_desktop;Docker;CFD_win32;nuget_release;Desktop;MEMI-Desktop;CellaLAB-Desktop</Configurations>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    
    <AutoGenerateBindingRedirects>true</AutoGenerateBindingRedirects>
	  <RemoveIntegerChecks>true</RemoveIntegerChecks>
	  <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
	  <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>http://scibasic.net/</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/xieguigang/sciBASIC</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageIcon>logo-knot.png</PackageIcon>
    <Version>1.0.9762.10518</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.9762.10518</AssemblyVersion>
    <Title>Low-Level Binary Data Stream Reader and Writer Toolkit</Title>
    <Description>Extends BinaryReader and BinaryWriter with endianness aware primitives, length-prefixed strings, BZip2 and LZW compression, XDR encoding and a Python pickle codec for parsing custom binary file formats, plus a Java style ByteBuffer.</Description>
    <AssemblyTitle>Microsoft.VisualBasic.Data.BinaryData</AssemblyTitle>
    <Authors>xieguigang &lt;I@xieguigang.me&gt;</Authors>
    <Company>sciBASIC.NET Foundation</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) sciBASIC.NET Foundation</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>scibasic;binary-data;binary-reader;endianness;bzip2;lzw;xdr;pickle;byte-buffer</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>The low level binary I/O toolkit of sciBASIC#. Reader and writer: BinaryDataReader and BinaryDataWriter extend BinaryReader and BinaryWriter with a switchable ByteOrder, the BinaryStringFormat string encodings (ByteLengthPrefix, WordLengthPrefix, DwordLengthPrefix, UInt32LengthPrefix and ZeroTerminated) and the BinaryDateTimeFormat date encodings, plus writer helpers such as ReserveOffset and TemporarySeek for back-patching offsets. Buffers: ByteBuffer implements Java style position / limit / flip / compact semantics with relative and absolute get and put, while BufferRegion describes a span inside a buffer. Compression: a fully managed BZip2 implementation (block compressor and decompressor, Huffman stages, MTF+RLE2, DivSufSort and CRC32) together with LZW Encoder and Decoder. Encodings: the Xdr namespace implements XDR (RFC 4506) packing and unpacking. Python interop: the Pickle namespace provides MinimalPicklePickler and MinimalPickleUnpickler which map Python tuple, set, complex and generic object graphs onto .NET types. These pieces are the foundation the other sciBASIC# binary format readers (HDF5, netCDF, SQLite3, HDSPack and Feather) are built on.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

